Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.70,0:00:05.20,Card,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,132)\fad(180,220)}“Agents triage every
Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.70,0:00:05.20,Card,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,196)\fad(180,220)}incoming PR and issue
Dialogue: 3,0:00:01.70,0:00:05.20,Card,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(540,260)\fad(180,220)}for security”
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.00,0:00:00.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,Yesterday
Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.20,0:00:01.38,Caption,,0,0,0,,we did a launch for our
Dialogue: 0,0:00:01.38,0:00:02.20,Caption,,0,0,0,,open source project
Dialogue: 0,0:00:02.20,0:00:03.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,Beacon, and we got like
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.82,0:00:05.58,Caption,,0,0,0,,an influx of dozens and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.58,0:00:06.82,Caption,,0,0,0,,dozens of PRs and
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.82,0:00:07.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,issues.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:07.48,0:00:09.69,Caption,,0,0,0,,And we have a security
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.69,0:00:11.53,Caption,,0,0,0,,agent and kind of like a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.53,0:00:13.63,Caption,,0,0,0,,code verification agent
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.63,0:00:14.49,Caption,,0,0,0,,try to put out like a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.49,0:00:15.99,Caption,,0,0,0,,remediation for the
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.99,0:00:17.77,Caption,,0,0,0,,issue, try to do like a
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.77,0:00:18.77,Caption,,0,0,0,,security stress test on
Dialogue: 0,0:00:18.77,0:00:21.01,Caption,,0,0,0,,the PR content.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.01,0:00:21.98,Caption,,0,0,0,,And then also look at
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.98,0:00:23.34,Caption,,0,0,0,,the author of the issue
Dialogue: 0,0:00:23.34,0:00:25.10,Caption,,0,0,0,,or the PR to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.10,0:00:26.08,Caption,,0,0,0,,trustworthiness.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:26.18,0:00:27.66,Caption,,0,0,0,,And so we're trying to
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.66,0:00:29.36,Caption,,0,0,0,,build systems to like
Dialogue: 0,0:00:29.36,0:00:30.46,Caption,,0,0,0,,really automatically
Dialogue: 0,0:00:30.46,0:00:32.21,Caption,,0,0,0,,determine like what are
Dialogue: 0,0:00:32.21,0:00:33.89,Caption,,0,0,0,,meaningful issues or
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.89,0:00:34.48,Caption,,0,0,0,,PRs.
